{"title":"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the beginning of the summer, Aidan was 160 cm tall. At the end of the summer, he measured his height again and discovered that it had increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fbf33b81900fa9e836a608be7484b4c4d6ea3ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />. Measured in cm, what was his height at the end of summer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c163db74d881a00c4f7c4f7c30412950df5c45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 168 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 165 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 160.8 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 172 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 170$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"456\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of centimeters that Aidan's height increased, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be his height after the summer. Using the fact that his original height was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b921eebe6fcb6019117772839fa2aa142827e703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and his height increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fbf33b81900fa9e836a608be7484b4c4d6ea3ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" /> of that, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b074961bc5c2d35e22a6c2621221dc57d443adc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5\\% \\times 160 = \\frac{1}{20} \\times 160 = 8 \\text{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"261\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b91307151003b477c7851a221f0831563ae0fa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = x + 160 = 8 + 160 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 168} \\text{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"299\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><